{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pulls/8641","id":4607423773,"node_id":"PR_kwDOMMa-Ps8AAAABEp-1HQ","html_url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pull/8641","diff_url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pull/8641.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pull/8641.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/issues/8641","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pulls/8641/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pulls/8641/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/issues/8641/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/statuses/3ddc4c33d31468f59be4aa0ae590d40612c5ac39","number":8641,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Type `None` in a list of output types as `| None` so `output_type=[Foo, Bar, None]` passes pyright","user":{"login":"DouweM","id":159434,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1OTQzNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/159434?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM","html_url":"https://github.com/DouweM","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"No existing issue: found in an audit of the `None`-route docs added in #8540.\n\n`output_type=[Ticket, Escalation, None]` works at runtime (and is documented in `docs/models/typesafe.md` and `docs/output.md`), but pyright rejected the bare `None` item. The agent then fell back to `Agent[object, str]`, even with explicit `Agent[object, Ticket | Escalation | None]` generics. `A | None` as a value already worked.\n\nAdding `None` to the `OutputSpec` item union would make the call type-check but silently drop `None` from the output type, because `type[T]` can't bind `T` from the value `None`. So a private `_NoneOutput[T]` protocol matches the `None` value structurally: `__class__` binds `T` to `None`, and `__bool__ -> Literal[False]` keeps `0`, `False`, `''` and the like out. It's accepted as an item of an `OutputSpec` sequence, in the `NativeOutput`/`PromptedOutput` `outputs` argument, and as `ToolOutput(None, ...)` (how the typesafe docs recommend naming the decline route); the public `outputs`/`output` fields keep their types. A bare `output_type=None` stays rejected, since it raises a `UserError` (and on `run()` means \"no override\").\n\n**New public surface:** none.\n\n**User-visible behavior** (pyright `reveal_type`):\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Agent(output_type=[A, B, None])` | error, `Agent[object, str]` | `Agent[object, A \\| B \\| None]` |\n| `Agent(output_type=[ToolOutput(A), None])` | error | `A \\| None` |\n| `Agent(output_type=[A, ToolOutput(None, name='nothing')])` | error | `A \\| None` |\n| `NativeOutput([A, None])` / `PromptedOutput([A, None])` | error | `A \\| None` |\n| `agent.run(..., output_type=[A, None]).output` (also `run_sync`, `run_stream`, `iter`) | error, `Unknown` | `A \\| None` |\n| `Agent(output_type=A \\| None)` | `A \\| None` | unchanged |\n| `Agent(output_type=None)` | error | error (unchanged) |\n\n**Verification:** `assert_type` pins in `tests/typed_agent.py`; they fail if the protocol is replaced with a plain `None` member. Four `# type: ignore[arg-type]` in `tests/models/test_typesafe.py` became unnecessary and are removed.\n\n**What changes for existing users:** code that already type-checks is unaffected. Code using `None` in an output list now type-checks, with `| None` in the output type.\n\nKnown gap: `[None]` alone type-checks but is refused at runtime.\n\n### Checklist\n\n- [ ] Any **AI generated code** has been reviewed line-by-line by the human PR author, who stands by it.\n- [x] No **breaking changes** in accordance with the [version policy](https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-ai/blob/main/docs/version-policy.md).\n- [x] Any permitted **compatibility impact** has a label, warning, migration, release note, and exact API-check waiver.\n- [x] **PR title** is fit for the [release changelog](https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-ai/releases).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pull/8641?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n\n","labels":[{"id":7110547176,"node_id":"LA_kwDOMMa-Ps8AAAABp9JW6A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"Report that something isn't working, or PR implementing a fix","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":9947550442,"node_id":"LA_kwDOMMa-Ps8AAAACUOuS6g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/labels/size:%20S","name":"size: S","description":"Small PR (≤100 weighted lines)","color":"0